---
import MagazineSectionHeading from '../components/MagazineSectionHeading.astro';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../styles/approved-pages.css';
---
<Layout title="Build real games" masthead={false}>
<div class="approved-page index-page">
<section class="game-feature" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
    <div class="feature-intro">
<h1 id="hero-title">You can <em>make these.</em>
</h1>
<p>Build real games. Learn what makes them work.<br> Explore different ideas, genres and ways to program across machines and languages.</p>
</div>
    <div class="game-art">
<figure class="capture" style="--capture-width:256px;--capture-height:240px"><img src="/images/learning/nes.png" width="256" height="240" alt="Dash on the NES, from the 6502 assembly course"><figcaption><strong>Can you time the jump?</strong><br>Dash · NES · 6502 assembly.</figcaption>
</figure>
</div>
    <div class="feature-name">
<h2>Different games.<br>Different possibilities.</h2>
</div>
    <div class="game-result">
<figure class="capture" style="--capture-width:416px;--capture-height:312px"><img src="/images/learning/c64.png" width="416" height="312" alt="Safe Cracker on the Commodore 64, from the BASIC course"><figcaption><strong>Can you crack the code?</strong><br>Safe Cracker · Commodore 64 · BASIC.</figcaption>
</figure>
</div>
    <div class="feature-copy">
<p>Dodge meteors, crack a code, guide sheep home or time a jump. Each game explores different ideas and the character of its machine.</p>
<div class="actions">
<a class="action" href="/start-here/"><span>Find your way in</span><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24" height="24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 12h15m-6-6 6 6-6 6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/></svg>
</a>
<a class="text-link" href="#systems">Choose your machine</a>
</div>
</div>
    </section>
<section class="system-routes magazine-section" id="systems" aria-labelledby="systems-title">
<div class="beginner-entry" id="beginner">
<div>
<h2>Never programmed before?</h2>
<p>Start with The Basics: give instructions, remember a value and ask for input. No machine or language to choose yet.</p>
</div>
<a class="action secondary" href="/foundations/basics/"><span>Start with The Basics</span><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24" height="24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 12h15m-6-6 6 6-6 6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/></svg>
</a>
</div>
<MagazineSectionHeading id="systems-title">
<Fragment slot="title">Different Machines.<br>Different Ways In.</Fragment>
Choose the machine or language that interests you. The Spectrum is one starting point; the C64, Amiga and NES have their own routes.
</MagazineSectionHeading>
<div class="system-route-list">
<article class="machine-route">
<a class="machine-choice" href="/systems/sinclair-zx-spectrum/"><img src="/images/learning/hardware-spectrum.png" width="2168" height="1593" loading="lazy" alt="ZX Spectrum 48K with its rubber keyboard and rainbow case stripe"><strong>ZX Spectrum</strong><span>BASIC · Z80 assembly</span>
</a>
<p class="photo-credit">Photograph supplied by the project.</p>
</article>
<article class="machine-route">
<a class="machine-choice" href="/systems/commodore-64/"><img src="/images/learning/hardware-c64.jpg" width="4600" height="2600" loading="lazy" alt="Commodore 64 breadbin computer with brown keys"><strong>Commodore 64</strong><span>BASIC · 6502 assembly</span>
</a>
<p class="photo-credit">Photo: <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Commodore-64-Computer-FR.jpg">Evan-Amos</a> · public domain.</p>
</article>
<article class="machine-route">
<a class="machine-choice" href="/systems/commodore-amiga/"><img src="/images/learning/hardware-amiga.jpg" width="1095" height="734" loading="lazy" alt="Commodore Amiga 500 Plus photographed on a white background"><strong>Commodore Amiga</strong><span>AMOS · Blitz BASIC · 68000 assembly</span>
</a>
<p class="photo-credit">Amiga 500 Plus · Photo: <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Amiga_500_Plus_(white_background).jpg">Sernot / Ubcule</a> · public domain.</p>
</article>
<article class="machine-route">
<a class="machine-choice" href="/systems/nintendo-entertainment-system/"><img src="/images/learning/hardware-nes.jpg" width="5560" height="3020" loading="lazy" alt="Nintendo Entertainment System console with its wired controller"><strong>Nintendo Entertainment System</strong><span>6502 assembly</span>
</a>
<p class="photo-credit">Photo: <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:NES-Console-Set.jpg">Evan-Amos</a> · public domain.</p>
</article>
</div>
<a class="text-link" href="/systems/">Explore the full systems directory</a>
</section>
<section class="learning magazine-section" id="learning" aria-labelledby="learning-title">
<MagazineSectionHeading id="learning-title">
<Fragment slot="title">Build Things.<br><em>Understand More.</em>
</Fragment>
Lessons guide the work. Shared subjects help you open the ideas behind it, and follow them beyond one game, language or machine. Start with the question you have.
</MagazineSectionHeading>
    <div class="learning-feature">
<div>
<h3>
<a href="/foundations/">Foundations</a>
</h3>
<p>Explore how programs work: decisions, repetition, structure, numbers and bits. Pseudocode, diagrams and experiments keep the idea separate from a language’s syntax.</p>
<a class="text-link" href="/foundations/counting-in-twos/">How can bits represent a number?</a>
</div>
<div class="learning-example">
<h4>The same bits. Two ways to read them.</h4><dl class="number-study">
<div><dt>Binary</dt><dd>00001010</dd>
</div>
<div><dt>Decimal</dt><dd>10</dd>
</div></dl>
<p>Representation is an idea you can take to every system.</p>
</div>
</div>
    <div class="learning-pair">
<article>
<figure class="capture" style="--capture-width:352px;--capture-height:296px"><img src="/images/learning/dice.png" width="352" height="296" alt="A BASIC dice experiment showing six counts and a coloured frequency chart"><figcaption>Roll, count, compare. A sample of 120 dice rolls.</figcaption>
</figure>
<h3>
<a href="/craft/maths-for-games/">Maths for Games</a>
</h3>
<p>Explore chance, direction and movement through experiments you can change. Build a dice experiment, compare sample sizes, or turn coordinates into an aimed shot.</p>
<a class="text-link" href="/craft/maths-for-games/">Explore chance and aiming</a>
</article>
<article>
<figure class="capture game-feel-preview" style="--capture-width:352px">
<div class="movement-preview">
<p class="movement-question">Hold right. Let go.</p><!-- Static comparison from the maintained Game Feel model, 144 fixed 1/60-second updates at top speed 240: right for 1.2 seconds, released for 1.2 seconds. No raster capture or simulated browser state. Source SVG track and ship geometry retained. -->
<div class="movement-lane">
<p><strong>Responsive</strong><span>Stopped</span>
</p><svg viewBox="0 0 900 90" role="img" aria-label="Responsive: stopped after releasing the control"><path class="track" d="M20 70H880"/><rect class="target" x="520" y="6" width="80" height="66"/><g transform="translate(428 40)"><path d="M-17-12H5L23 0 5 12H-17L-10 0Z"/></g></svg><span class="movement-marker">Marker</span>
</div>
<div class="movement-lane">
<p><strong>Slippery</strong><span>Still moving</span>
</p><svg viewBox="0 0 900 90" role="img" aria-label="Slippery: still moving after releasing the control"><path class="track" d="M20 70H880"/><rect class="target" x="520" y="6" width="80" height="66"/><g transform="translate(618.9000000000005 40)"><path d="M-17-12H5L23 0 5 12H-17L-10 0Z"/></g></svg><span class="movement-marker">Marker</span>
</div>
<div class="movement-lane">
<p><strong>Heavy</strong><span>Stopped</span>
</p><svg viewBox="0 0 900 90" role="img" aria-label="Heavy: stopped after releasing the control"><path class="track" d="M20 70H880"/><rect class="target" x="520" y="6" width="80" height="66"/><g transform="translate(311.3666666666666 40)"><path d="M-17-12H5L23 0 5 12H-17L-10 0Z"/></g></svg><span class="movement-marker">Marker</span>
</div>
</div><figcaption>The same input, three responses. A moment from the Game Feel comparison.</figcaption>
</figure>
<h3>
<a href="/craft/">The Craft</a>
</h3>
<p>Make deliberate choices about how a game plays. Explore controls, movement and feedback, then test what changing one rule does to the experience.</p>
<a class="text-link" href="/experiments/game-feel/index.html">Try the Game Feel playground</a>
</article>
</div>
    <article class="vault-moment">
<div>
<h3>
<a href="/vault/techniques/colour-clash/">Why do the colours clash?</a>
</h3>
<p>A tiny sprite meets an eight-pixel colour cell. Follow the trade-off from the screen into the hardware that makes it happen.</p>
<a class="text-link" href="/vault/techniques/colour-clash/">Explore colour clash in the Vault</a>
</div>
<figure class="capture" style="--capture-width:1076px;--capture-height:446px"><img src="/images/learning/colour-clash.png" width="1076" height="446" alt="Two diagrams show a white sprite meeting a red brick wall: either the sprite or the wall supplies the cell colour."><figcaption>One cell, competing colours. The sprite or the background supplies the ink.</figcaption>
</figure>
</article>
    <div class="learning-library">
<a href="/patterns/"><strong>Pattern Library</strong><span>Find techniques you can adapt, with their assumptions and trade-offs.</span>
</a>
<a href="/vault/"><strong>The Vault</strong><span>Explore the machines, people and circumstances behind the software.</span>
</a>
<a href="/timeline/"><strong>Timeline</strong><span>Place the machines and their ideas in computing history.</span>
</a>
</div>
<p class="entry-note">Shared subjects are useful places to enter or return to. They are not a compulsory course to finish before making a game.</p>
</section>
<section class="system-games magazine-section" aria-labelledby="games-title">
<MagazineSectionHeading id="games-title">
<Fragment slot="title">Same Curiosity.<br><em>Different Possibilities.</em>
</Fragment>
See how the lessons use each machine’s character. These are captures from the current courses, rather than a promise that every route has the same coverage.
</MagazineSectionHeading>
<article class="system-game" style="--capture-width:768px">
<div class="system-game-copy">
<h3>Safe Cracker</h3>
<p class="target">Commodore 64 · BASIC</p>
<p>Can you crack the code? Make a guess, read the clues and narrow the search.</p>
<p class="game-learning">Learn variables, decisions and repetition.</p>
<a class="action" href="/systems/commodore-64/basic/safe-cracker/"><span>Explore Safe Cracker</span><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24" height="24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 12h15m-6-6 6 6-6 6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/></svg>
</a>
</div>
<figure class="capture system-capture"><img src="/images/learning/c64.png" width="416" height="312" alt="Safe Cracker, a real Commodore 64 · BASIC curriculum capture"><figcaption>Safe Cracker · original course capture, 416 × 312.</figcaption>
</figure>
</article>
<article class="system-game" style="--capture-width:768px">
<div class="system-game-copy">
<h3>Dash</h3>
<p class="target">NES · 6502 assembly</p>
<p>Can you time the jump? Read the controller, avoid the hazard and gather coins.</p>
<p class="game-learning">Learn controller input, movement and collisions.</p>
<a class="action" href="/systems/nintendo-entertainment-system/assembly/dash/"><span>Explore Dash</span><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24" height="24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 12h15m-6-6 6 6-6 6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/></svg>
</a>
</div>
<figure class="capture system-capture"><img src="/images/learning/nes.png" width="256" height="240" alt="Dash, a real NES · 6502 assembly curriculum capture"><figcaption>Dash · original course capture, 256 × 240.</figcaption>
</figure>
</article>
<article class="system-game" style="--capture-width:768px">
<div class="system-game-copy">
<h3>Flock</h3>
<p class="target">Commodore Amiga · 68000 assembly</p>
<p>Can you get the flock home? Dodge the traffic, cross the stream and fill the fold.</p>
<p class="game-learning">Learn hardware sprites, collisions and game states.</p>
<a class="action" href="/systems/commodore-amiga/assembly/flock/"><span>Explore Flock</span><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24" height="24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 12h15m-6-6 6 6-6 6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/></svg>
</a>
</div>
<figure class="capture system-capture"><img src="/images/learning/amiga.png" width="768" height="576" alt="Flock, a real Commodore Amiga · 68000 assembly curriculum capture"><figcaption>Flock · original course capture, 768 × 576.</figcaption>
</figure>
</article>
</section>
<section class="first-step magazine-section" id="first-step" aria-labelledby="first-title">
<div>
<h2 id="first-title">One Game.<br>One Small <em>First Step.</em>
</h2>
<p>Meteor Storm’s first lesson moves pixels across a byte boundary. A bit that leaves one byte must arrive in the next. That small idea is the beginning of the ship’s movement.</p>
<a class="action" href="/systems/sinclair-zx-spectrum/assembly/meteor-storm/unit-01/"><span>Start Meteor Storm</span><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24" height="24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 12h15m-6-6 6 6-6 6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/></svg>
</a>
</div>
<div class="pixel-study">
<h3>Carry a pixel into the next byte</h3><pre aria-label="Two bytes before and after shifting right"><span>Before</span>  10000001 00000000{'\n'}<span>After</span>   01000000 10000000</pre>
<p>The rightmost bit crosses the boundary. Nothing gets lost.</p>
<a class="text-link" href="/systems/sinclair-zx-spectrum/assembly/meet-assembly/">New to assembly? Begin with Meet Assembly</a>
</div>
</section>
<section class="closing-invitation magazine-section" id="start" aria-labelledby="start-title">
<MagazineSectionHeading id="start-title" ending="none">
<Fragment slot="title">What Will<br><em>You Make?</em>
</Fragment>
New to programming? Begin with The Basics. Have a machine in mind? Choose its route and find something you want to make.
</MagazineSectionHeading>
<div class="actions">
<a class="action" href="/foundations/basics/"><span>Start with The Basics</span><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24" height="24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 12h15m-6-6 6 6-6 6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/></svg>
</a>
<a class="action secondary" href="#systems"><span>Choose your machine</span><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24" height="24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 12h15m-6-6 6 6-6 6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/></svg>
</a>
</div>
</section>
</div>
</Layout>
